    {
      "value": "<p>A chain of low islands at the cold end of the flats, most of them under a metre of water at the top of the tide. Tall weathered posts stand in rows off the seaward shores, replaced often enough that none of them is old. The survey has never landed here and views the islands from the water, at a distance agreed in 2291 and not since renegotiated.</p>",
